Compendium of NetHack Trivia

Couldn't sleep nights? Constantly contemplating zapping that wand of
polymorph at your boss? Wondering where your blessed greased bag of
holding goes in the daytime? Well, this is the right place for you!
It's very simple. Answer the trivia questions, and rack up points.
Occaisionally I might post a few puzzlers like before, but those
weren't very popular. (1)
I'll try to keep the trivia restricted to this topic/thread, so you'll
know where to go to for scores and new questions. Please don't cheat by
looking at the spoilers (or others' responses); if you don't know the
answer, don't spoil it for someone else. If you do, post it, of course.
When you do reply, try to make it as intelligent as possible. Extra
credit is given for interesting responses.
Ok, so let's begin.

Trivia Set #001

Topic: Confessions
(In these riddles, guess who [or what] is describing themselves. There
may be more than one correct answer.)

Level: Easy (3 points)
1. I am the dead that may give you new life.
2. His eyes will be wide; who covets my hide.
3. No one will like your taste with my magic upon you.
4. Fear not Medusa with me in your hand.
5. For my corpse is always left / Of goodly art the world is bereft.

Level: Medium (5 points)
1. You'll find me in Kansas, but with me you won't make it to Oz.
2. Make with me no illegal move.
3. Who do you think you are... my dentist?
4. I am a sharp meal but a good chew.
5. I will make you one with me, so long as you keep your cool.
6. More than a few stings will be my cost; a vegan wouldn't dare it.
7. Pitiful.. but not before me.
8. I am the light that you might eat, but won't you keep your conducts?
9. Xorn, you may eat me, but you do not need me.
10. A certain wet rattle of mine / At the cost of the sight of thine.

Level: Difficult (8 points)
1. As the DevTeam will tell you, I am the loyalest of dogs.
2. Fear my wrath, for Magicbane is my blade, though to Aegypt I have
never been.
3. Turn the tap on greater, or else lose me.
4. Find me with my bretheren in the swamp, where we guard our sunken
treasure.
5. I made the bane / of Ichabod Crane.

Level: Bonus (points vary)
1. I'm said to be quite stunning, and a kiss with me is out of this
world.
2. Stick with me; didn't you find me attractive at first sight?
3. Excuse me for grabbing onto bare men; they don't appreciate it.
4. Oft do I suck their juices; those round things that my tentacles
grab.
5. It might be shocking when I grab onto unlubricated visitors.

Topic: Contributions
(essay time!)
1. Which class do you think is the easiest to play, and why?
2. Consider the choice of genociding spellcasters versus powerful melee
monsters.
3. Evaluate the usefulness of chaotic artifacts.

Topic: Choices
(multiple choice -- get that #2 pencil ready!)
1. Which of the following cannot rise from debris?
a) earth elemental
b) air elemental
c) paper golem
d) glass golem
e) skeleton

2. Which of the following are not always found guarding Fort Ludios?
a) a moat
b) an army
c) land mines
d) bear traps
e) dragons

3. Which of the following has a sickness attack?
a) Orcus
b) the Wizard of Yendor
c) Vlad the Impaler
d) Demogorgon
e) violet fungi

4. Which of the following is vulnerable to the finger of death?
a) silver dragon
b) Pestilence
c) Vlad the Impaler
d) grey dragon
e) horned devil

5. How much wood could a woodchuck chuck if a woodchuck could chuck
wood?
a) a lot
b) none
c) a little
d) some
e) ZOT!

